---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "@/components/Icon.astro";
import { site } from "@/data/site";
import { withBase } from "@/lib/url";
---

<Base
  title="Optical Tissue Classification"
  description="A physics-informed neural network classifying 25 tissue types from three-wavelength diffuse reflectance spectroscopy with confidence-gated inference."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pt-36 pb-24 sm:px-12 md:px-24">
    <a
      href={withBase("/#projects")}
      class="font-mono text-muted hover:text-accent inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs transition-colors"
    >
      <Icon name="arrow" size={14} class="rotate-180" /> back to portfolio
    </a>

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mt-8 mb-12" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">BMEN 5421 · University of Minnesota · Spring 2025</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Optical Tissue Classification</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-2 text-lg">Neural Classification of Tissue Type via Multispectral Diffuse Reflectance Spectroscopy</p>
      <p class="text-body mt-3 text-sm">
        Mitchell Salzman
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">
        Course: Introduction to Biomedical Optics (BMEN 5421)
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Architecture Diagram -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-white">
        <img
          src={withBase("/media/optical-architecture.svg")}
          alt="Optical tissue classification architecture: fiber-optic probe measures reflectance at three wavelengths, features feed into MLP classifier, outputs tissue type with confidence gating"
          class="block w-full p-4"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Problem -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">The Problem</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        During surgery, distinguishing healthy tissue from tumor is life-or-death. Leave
        tumor behind and it recurs, cut too far and you damage critical structures. Today
        that call rests on frozen-section pathology: a 20 to 30 minute wait mid-operation while
        a pathologist examines a slice under a microscope. An intraoperative probe that could
        classify tissue in real time from its optical signature would give surgeons immediate
        feedback without stopping the procedure.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-accent text-lg font-bold">25</p>
          <p class="text-accent mt-1 text-xs font-medium">Tissue classes</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-heading text-lg font-bold">3</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Wavelengths</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-heading text-lg font-bold">83.6%</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Confident accuracy</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-heading text-lg font-bold">&lt;1 ms</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Inference time</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 text-center text-xs">
        A physics-informed forward model generates synthetic training data; a confidence gate ensures the classifier only speaks when it's sure
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Pipeline Overview -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Pipeline</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        The system chains a physics-based forward model with a machine learning classifier.
        Rather than collecting thousands of real tissue measurements, the forward model
        simulates what a three-wavelength probe would read for each tissue type, then the
        neural network learns to invert that mapping.
      </p>

      <div class="mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
        <h3 class="text-heading mb-4 text-base font-semibold">Four-Stage Pipeline</h3>
        <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">1. Absorption</p>
            <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">
              Beer-Lambert law computes absorption from five chromophore concentrations
              (HbO<sub>2</sub>, HbR, water, lipid, melanin) at each wavelength.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">2. Scattering</p>
            <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">
              Mie scattering power law models reduced scattering using tissue-specific
              amplitude and exponent parameters.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">3. Reflectance</p>
            <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">
              The Farrell-Patterson-Wilson diffusion approximation converts optical
              properties into the diffuse reflectance a probe would measure.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">4. Classification</p>
            <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">
              An MLP classifier trained on 50,000 synthetic samples maps the 6D feature
              vector to one of 25 tissue labels, gated by confidence.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Physics Forward Model -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Physics Forward Model</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        Each tissue type is defined by its chromophore composition and scattering parameters,
        drawn from published optical-property literature. The forward model computes what a
        660 nm / 810 nm / 940 nm probe would read through three physical laws.
      </p>

      <div class="mb-8 space-y-4">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading text-base font-semibold">Beer-Lambert Absorption</h3>
          <p class="text-body mt-2 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed">
            Absorption coefficient &mu;<sub>a</sub>(&lambda;) is the weighted sum of each
            chromophore's extinction coefficient times its concentration. Five chromophores
            (oxyhemoglobin, deoxyhemoglobin, water, lipid, and melanin) cover the
            dominant absorbers in biological tissue.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading text-base font-semibold">Mie Scattering Power Law</h3>
          <p class="text-body mt-2 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed">
            Reduced scattering &mu;<sub>s</sub>&prime;(&lambda;) = a &middot; (&lambda; / 500 nm)<sup>-b</sup>,
            where a captures scattering amplitude and b encodes particle size. Higher b
            means smaller scatterers, typical of cellular structures.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading text-base font-semibold">Diffusion Approximation</h3>
          <p class="text-body mt-2 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed">
            The Farrell-Patterson-Wilson model (1992) combines absorption and scattering
            into a closed-form estimate of diffuse reflectance R<sub>d</sub> at a given
            source-detector separation, producing the signal a real probe would measure.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tissue Classes -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Tissue Coverage</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        The model classifies across 25 tissue types spanning eight organ sites, plus
        structural tissues that a probe might encounter during surgery. Compositions are
        sourced from peer-reviewed optical property measurements.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Brain</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Gray matter, white matter, low-grade glioma, high-grade glioma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Breast</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Fibroglandular, adipose, carcinoma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Colon</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Normal mucosa, carcinoma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Skin</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Epidermis, dermis, melanoma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Liver</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Normal parenchyma, hepatic tumor</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Lung</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Normal tissue, carcinoma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Oral / Head & Neck</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Normal mucosa, squamous cell carcinoma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Kidney</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Normal cortex, renal cell carcinoma</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4">
          <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold">Structural</p>
          <p class="text-body mt-1 text-[0.85rem]">Adipose, skeletal muscle, whole blood, bone, aorta wall</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Synthetic Data Generation -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Synthetic Data Generation</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        Rather than requiring thousands of real tissue samples, the forward model generates
        realistic training data by running each tissue's composition through the physics
        pipeline with two layers of noise that mimic real measurement conditions.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading mb-3 text-base font-semibold">Noise Model</h3>
          <dl class="text-body space-y-3 text-[0.9rem]">
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Biological variation:</dt>
              <dd class="inline"> &plusmn;15% perturbation of chromophore concentrations to simulate inter-patient differences</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Multiplicative noise:</dt>
              <dd class="inline"> &sigma; = 0.08, modeling probe contact and illumination variability</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Additive noise:</dt>
              <dd class="inline"> &sigma; = 0.005, modeling detector read noise</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading mb-3 text-base font-semibold">Feature Engineering</h3>
          <dl class="text-body space-y-3 text-[0.9rem]">
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Raw reflectances:</dt>
              <dd class="inline"> R<sub>660</sub>, R<sub>810</sub>, R<sub>940</sub></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Reflectance ratios:</dt>
              <dd class="inline"> R<sub>660</sub>/R<sub>810</sub>, R<sub>810</sub>/R<sub>940</sub>, R<sub>660</sub>/R<sub>940</sub></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Total samples:</dt>
              <dd class="inline"> 50,000 (2,000 per class), 80/20 train/test split</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Model Architecture -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Model Architecture</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        The classifier is a two-hidden-layer MLP trained with Adam and early stopping.
        The architecture is deliberately simple. The physics forward model does the heavy
        lifting, so the neural network only needs to learn the inverse mapping from a
        well-structured 6D feature space.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
        <h3 class="text-heading mb-3 text-base font-semibold">Architecture Details</h3>
        <dl class="text-body space-y-3 text-[0.9rem]">
          <div>
            <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Type:</dt>
            <dd class="inline"> Multi-layer perceptron (scikit-learn MLPClassifier)</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Layers:</dt>
            <dd class="inline"> Input(6) &rarr; Dense(128, ReLU) &rarr; Dense(128, ReLU) &rarr; Softmax(25)</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Optimizer:</dt>
            <dd class="inline"> Adam, learning rate 0.001, batch size 256</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Regularization:</dt>
            <dd class="inline"> Early stopping with 10% validation holdout, patience 15 epochs</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Convergence:</dt>
            <dd class="inline"> 46 epochs</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)] inline">Preprocessing:</dt>
            <dd class="inline"> StandardScaler normalization for gradient stability</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Results -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Results</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        The raw 25-class accuracy is 35.0%, modest for fine-grained tissue discrimination
        with only three wavelengths. But the confusion matrix reveals that errors cluster
        among tissues with similar optical properties, not random misclassifications. The
        confidence gate is what makes the system clinically useful.
      </p>

      <div class="mb-8 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)]">
        <img
          src={withBase("/media/optical-confusion-matrix.png")}
          alt="Normalized confusion matrix across 25 tissue classes showing 35% overall accuracy with strong diagonal for distinct tissues"
          class="w-full bg-white p-2"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <p class="text-muted bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] py-2 text-center text-xs">
          Normalized confusion matrix with color-coded bars showing healthy (green), tumor (red), and structural (blue) classes
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-accent text-lg font-bold">35.0%</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Overall accuracy</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-accent text-lg font-bold">83.6%</p>
          <p class="text-accent mt-1 text-xs font-medium">Confident accuracy</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-heading text-lg font-bold">95%+</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Blood & bone recall</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-heading text-lg font-bold">8</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Organ sites covered</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
        <h3 class="text-heading mb-3 text-base font-semibold">Healthy vs. Tumor Discrimination</h3>
        <p class="text-body mb-4 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed">
          Even when the model confuses subtypes within an organ, it usually gets the
          healthy-vs-tumor binary call right, the clinically critical distinction.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4">
          {[
            { organ: "Breast", acc: "76.3%" },
            { organ: "Lung", acc: "70.2%" },
            { organ: "Skin", acc: "66.8%" },
            { organ: "Brain", acc: "66.3%" },
            { organ: "Oral", acc: "59.1%" },
            { organ: "Colon", acc: "57.9%" },
            { organ: "Liver", acc: "55.1%" },
            { organ: "Kidney", acc: "51.7%" },
          ].map(({ organ, acc }) => (
            <div class="rounded border border-[var(--color-line)] px-3 py-2 text-center">
              <p class="text-heading text-sm font-semibold">{acc}</p>
              <p class="text-muted text-xs">{organ}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Confidence Gating -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Confidence Gating</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        The key design choice: rather than trusting every prediction, the system only reports
        a diagnosis when the softmax confidence exceeds 0.65. Low-confidence samples are
        flagged for pathologist review. This operationalizes the asymmetric cost structure
        of surgery. A wrong answer is far worse than saying "I'm not sure."
      </p>

      <div class="mb-8 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)]">
        <img
          src={withBase("/media/optical-confidence-analysis.png")}
          alt="Confidence distribution and accuracy vs threshold analysis showing 83.6% accuracy above the 0.65 operating point"
          class="w-full bg-white p-2"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <p class="text-muted bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] py-2 text-center text-xs">
          Left: confidence distribution on the test set. Right: accuracy climbs sharply as the threshold filters out uncertain predictions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-accent text-2xl font-bold">0.65</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Confidence threshold</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-accent text-2xl font-bold">12.4%</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Samples classified with confidence</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-accent text-2xl font-bold">83.6%</p>
          <p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Accuracy on those samples</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Insight -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Key Insight</h2>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
        <p class="text-body text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
          Three wavelengths can't resolve 25 tissues, but they don't need to. The
          physics-informed approach means the model doesn't learn arbitrary patterns; it
          learns to invert a physical process. And confidence gating means it doesn't
          have to be right about everything. It just has to know when it's sure. The
          tissues it classifies confidently (whole blood, bone, melanoma, high-grade glioma)
          are the ones with the most distinctive optical signatures, which is exactly
          what you'd want a real-time surgical probe to catch first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Future Work -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Future Work</h2>
      <ul class="text-body space-y-3 text-[0.95rem]">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent mt-2 block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current"></span>
          Add more wavelengths (e.g. 5-channel or hyperspectral) to increase separability between optically similar tissues
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent mt-2 block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current"></span>
          Validate against real tissue measurements using a bench-top spectrometer and ex vivo samples
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent mt-2 block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current"></span>
          Replace the MLP with a deeper architecture or ensemble to improve fine-grained discrimination
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent mt-2 block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current"></span>
          Incorporate spatial or time-resolved reflectance to separate absorption from scattering more cleanly
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent mt-2 block h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current"></span>
          Design a compact fiber-optic probe prototype for intraoperative testing
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Resources -->
    <section class="mb-8" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Resources</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href={withBase("/media/optical-confusion-matrix.png")}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-heading)] transition-colors hover:border-[var(--color-accent)]"
        >
          <Icon name="external" size={14} />
          Confusion Matrix
        </a>
        <a
          href={withBase("/media/optical-confidence-analysis.png")}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-heading)] transition-colors hover:border-[var(--color-accent)]"
        >
          <Icon name="external" size={14} />
          Confidence Analysis
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tech chips -->
    <div class="border-line flex flex-wrap gap-3 border-t pt-8" data-reveal>
      {["Python", "Scikit-learn", "MLP", "NumPy", "Matplotlib", "Beer-Lambert", "Diffusion Approximation", "Biomedical Optics"].map(t => (
        <span class="chip">{t}</span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
